  "english": "THE SEVEN-WEEK CYCLE OF THE ROMANS [Roman Calendar]\n\nJuly\n\n30. Monday. Tone 4 [Dkh / ԴՁ]. Cyprian the Bishop, and the others. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 2 [Bk / բկ]: \"We bless\" (Orhnemk).\n\n31. Tuesday. Tone 4 [Dk / ԴԿ]. Athenogenes the Bishop, and the others. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 2 [Bk / բկ]: \"Who in the conflict\" (Ork i marti).\n\nAugust\n\n1. Wednesday. Tone 1 [Ah / ԱՁ]. Canticle of the Fathers of Repentance [Harst aghts.] Tone 2 [Bk / բկ]: \"Who didst save\" (Or apreguts'er).\n\n2. Thursday. Tone 1 [Ak / ԱԿ]. The Holy Forefathers: Adam, Abel, and the others.\n\n4. Saturday. Tone 2 [Bk / ԲԿ]. The sons and grandsons of the Enlightener [St. Gregory].\n\n5. Sunday. Tone 3 [Gz / ԳՁ]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [Gk / գկ]: \"Today He was sacrificed\" (Aysor zenao). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [Gz / գձ]: \"To the voice\" (I dzayn).\n\n6. Monday. Tone 3 [Gk / ԳԿ]. The Maccabees, Eleazar, and the others. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [Gz / գձ]: \"Who the torments\" (Ork ztanjanatsn).\n\n7. Tuesday. Tone 4 [Dz / ԴՁ]. The Twelve Prophets: Hosea, and the others.\n\n8. Wednesday. Tone 4 [Dk / ԴԿ]. Canticle of the Fathers of Repentance [Harst aghts.] Tone 3 [Gz / բձ]: \"Who art awesome\" (Or ahavor).\n\n9. Thursday. Tone 1 [Ah / ԱՁ]. Sophia and her three daughters. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 4 [Dk / դկ]: \"Those who hoped\" (Husats'ealkn).\n\n11. Saturday. Tone 2 [Dz / ԲՁ]. Thaddeus the Apostle and Sandukht the Virgin.\n\n12. Sunday. Tone 2 [Bk / ԲԿ]. Fifth [Sunday]. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [Bk / բկ]: \"The Resurrection of Christ\" (Zharut'iun K'ristosi). Fast-Breaking [Barekendan] of the Catechumens [Arachavorats].\n\n13. Monday. Tone 3 [Gz / ԳՁ]. Fast of the Catechumens [Arachavorats]. Canticle of the Fathers of Repentance [Harst aghts.] Tone 2 [Bk / բկ]: \"Blessed art Thou, Lord, God of our fathers\" (Harts'n merots' orhneal es Ter).\n\n14. Tuesday. Tone 3 [Gk / ԳԿ]. Of the Fast. Presentation of the Lord [Tearndaraj].\n\nMarch\n\n5. Sunday. Tone 4 [Dk / ԴԿ]. Great Fast-Breaking [Bun Barekendan]. See also the others according to their order in the First Volume, following the order of this place.\n\nJanuary\n\n6. Friday. Tone 4 [Dz / ԴՁ]. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ. The interval of eating [non-fasting days] is thirty-eight days.\n\n14. Saturday. Tone 4 [Dkh / ԴՁ]. John the Forerunner.\n\n15. Sunday. Tone 4 [Dk / ԴԿ]. First [Sunday]. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [Dk / դկ]: \"Glory to the Resurrection\" (P'ark' harut'ean).\n\n16. Monday. Tone 1 [Ah / ԱՁ]. Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.\n\n17. Tuesday. Tone 1 [Ak / ԱԿ]. Anthony, and Tryphon, Barsama, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n\n18. Wednesday. Tone 2 [Dz / ԲՁ]. Canticle of the Fathers of Repentance [Harst aghts.] Tone 1 [Ah / աձ]: \"The youths sang\" (Ergein mankunkn).\n\n19. Thursday. Tone 2 [Bk / ԲԿ]. Theodosius the King, and the Holy Children of Ephesus.\n\n21. Saturday. Tone 3 [Gk / ԳԿ]. Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril.\n\n22. Sunday. Tone 4 [Dz / ԴՁ]. Second [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 2 [Bk / բկ]: \"With voluntary\" (Kamavorut'eamb). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [Dz / դձ]: \"The resurrection of the Son of God\" (Zharut'iun astuatsorduoyn).\n\n23. Monday. Tone 4 [Dk / ԴԿ]. Cyriacus and Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 1 [Ak / ակ]: \"Who art most high\" (Or bardzreald es).\n\n24. Tuesday. Tone 1 [Ah / ԱՁ]. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenie the Virgin, and the others. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [Gz / գձ]: \"Without malice\" (Anokhakal).\n\n26. Thursday. Tone 2 [Dz / ԲՁ]. Eugenius, Macarius, and the others. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 2 [Dz / բձ]: \"With Thy saints\" (End surbs k'o).\n\n28. Saturday. Tone 3 [Gz / ԳՁ]. Gregory the Theologian.\n\n29. Sunday. Tone 3 [Gk / ԳԿ]. Third [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [Gz / գձ]: \"Creator of creatures\" (Ararichd araratsots'). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [Gk / գկ]: \"A vision like lightning\" (Tesil p'aylaknadzev). Because for the songs written above following Transfiguration [Vardavar], see the First Volume, but for the Canticles of the Sundays and Fast days, and for the Tones, see here.",
